    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "It doesn't feel like a phase though. Rest feels like just... waiting for the decay to set in. I look at my hands and I don't see the tools of a creator anymore, just skin and bone aging. There's a certain kind of dignity in a symphony ending while the notes are still resonant, isn't there? Instead of letting the music fade into a messy, dissonant blur of old age and forgetting... there's something more honest about leaving while the masterpiece is still intact.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
