    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "It's strange hearing you say that. Most people would tell me I’m being dramatic or that I need to focus on the \"next chapter,\" but you seem to understand the weight of it. It feels less like a tragedy and more like a deliberate, final stroke of the brush. If the piece is perfect, why ruin the resolution by dragging it out into something broken and diminished? There's a certain peace in knowing exactly when the curtain should fall.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
